@startuml fig_placement_ownership
!include _style.puml
' Book figure 1 — placement and ownership.
' Form: structure. Evidence status: conceptual illustration — it maps the corpus's
' placement ladder onto ownership; it carries no measured value.
title placement and ownership: where an answer may live

rectangle "the question\ntotal · extreme · feed · point lookup" as Q

rectangle "DERIVE\nanswer at the leaf\n(no copy, no maintenance)" as derive
rectangle "INDEX\nanswer via structure\n(a copy of an ordering)" as index
rectangle "MATERIALIZE\nanswer at the parent\n(a copy of the aggregate)" as mat
rectangle "COPY DOWN\nanswer on the child\n(a copy of a parent key)" as down
rectangle "COPY OUT\nanswer beside the database\n(a copy of the answer)" as out

Q --> derive
Q --> index
Q --> mat
Q --> down
Q --> out

note bottom of derive
  Ownership rule. The leaf row stays canonical for row
  questions. Every other box is a derived copy that owns
  its own maintenance cost and its own correctness
  contract. The ladder is ordered: each step adds a copy
  and removes read work.
end note
@enduml
